    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d122">

                <pb facs="0521" n="401" sameAs="frus:frus1922v01/pg401"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">800.51 W 89 Poland/3: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Minister in Poland</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Gibson</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Warsaw</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1922-06-09T18:00:00+01:00"><hi rendition="#italic">June 9, 1922—6
                                p.m.</hi></date><lb/>[Received June 10—7:47
                    p.m.]</dateline></opener>
                <p>59. Department’s June 3, 10 a.m. Foreign Office states Gliwic<anchor n="21"
                        xml:id="d122-f1"/> instructed by the Minister of Finance on May 6 to
                    represent Poland in the World War Foreign Debt Commission.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Gibson</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d122-f1" n="21" xml:id="d122-f1-content">
                <p>Hipolit Gliwic, commercial counselor of the Polish Legation at Washington.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
